WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.127
Cleaning does not end when the code finishes running.

00:00:03.127 --> 00:00:10.707
You need to verify that the result actually matches the rules you intended to apply.

00:00:10.707 --> 00:00:12.787
Recheck duplicates. Recount missing values.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:16.982
Inspect the data types. Look at category values.

00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:22.425
Count rule violations. Compare the number of rows before and after cleaning.

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:27.149
The code on this slide demonstrates simple quality checks.

00:00:27.149 --> 00:00:32.999
In larger projects, these checks can become functions or automated tests.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:39.264
For example, you might assert that order IDs are unique, that amount is never negative,

00:00:39.264 --> 00:00:43.259
or that satisfaction values stay between one and five.

00:00:43.259 --> 00:00:49.294
The important idea is that successful execution is not proof of correctness.

00:00:49.294 --> 00:00:54.929
A program can run perfectly and still produce a logically wrong dataset.

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:57.869
Always validate the result after cleaning.
